From c67ba1eeb71bb11e385a835fa333a4cb18bba4ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sramya <sramya@ami.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Apr 2026 19:05:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] add BMC firmware auto-recovery support

What this patch does:
 - Adds Kconfig defaults and environment variables for BMC auto-recovery.
 - When recovery_current_bootretry exceeds recovery_max_bootretry, checks
	 recovery_mode_selection=auto/mmc/tftp to determine the recovery source.
 - In auto mode, tries eMMC first and TFTP on the next boot if eMMC fails;
	 mmc and tftp directly use their respective recovery source.
 - Restores SPI using the recovery/golden image from the configured eMMC device
	 and partition (recovery_mmc_dev/recovery_mmc_part).
 - Uses recovery_bootfile as the eMMC image name and TFTP file path; TFTP server
	 configuration is provided by recovery_tftp_ip and includes DHCP setup.
 - Configures retry count (recovery_retry), boot retry state
	 (recovery_current_bootretry/recovery_max_bootretry), and the last recovery
	 source (recovery_last_source).
 - Writes the recovery image to SPI starting at offset 0x0, performing a
	 complete SPI update.
 - Disables hardware ABR when software BMC auto-recovery is enabled.
